{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "mms_sections",
    "description": "The ONE test size grid shared by every MMS problem and AST fixture of grids/sectional_volume_1d -- a fixture template library (not a lintable library entry; grids/*/mesh/ holds fixture geometry, schema-validated only), so the edge map is written once instead of once per consuming model. `mms_sections_vb` is the geometric edge array of NBIN sections spanning one doubling of particle volume, vb[kn] = 2^((kn-1)/NBIN) for kn = 1..NBIN+1 (vb[1] = 1, vb[NBIN+1] = 2; every section has the same volume ratio 2^(1/NBIN), the spacing sectional aerosol models use, so the sections WIDEN with v and the MMS exercises a nonuniform grid). It is spelled against the grid's metaparameter name NBIN so a loader-API or import-edge rebinding of NBIN re-derives the whole size grid consistently; a consuming model defines its edge observed as vb = mms_sections_vb(). Build-time positions (ic, 6.6.5 references) cannot apply this template -- they fold the edges from literals and NBIN inline (AGENTS.md build-time scope caveat).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:mesh-data",
      "family:sectional",
      "grid:sectional_volume_1d",
      "mesh:geometric"
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "mms_sections_vb": {
      "params": [],
      "description": "Section edge volumes of the geometric test grid: vb[kn] = 2^((kn - 1)/NBIN) over kn in bin_nodes.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "output_idx": ["kn"],
        "args": [],
        "ranges": {"kn": {"from": "bin_nodes"}},
        "expr": {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [2, {"op": "/", "args": [{"op": "-", "args": ["kn", 1]}, "NBIN"]}]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
